  "limitations": "This is component qualification, not completed automatic membership, release or capacity qualification. Authenticated inspection/capacity, owned automatic reconciliation, six-node repair without business traffic and balancing remain required. The original seven MR-11 names are unchanged: five exist; automatic_no_traffic_repair and leader_balance_with_lag remain absent. All 19 commands and 217 unique Rust cases pass on this source; five ignored child entry points run through owning parents. Current public Node coverage is its affected Raft lifecycle case. The separate 5751f36 regression record retains all 359 Rust passes including 88 public Node cases, and honestly records its one failed Clippy check; that error-propagation cleanup is fixed and Clippy passes here. The clean 5751f36 checkpoint pair also passed 1,000 serial repetitions, separately counted. Directory restarts are orderly actual Node instances with fresh process generations/ports; supersession is a canonical trusted observation, without claiming a second legitimate live owner. The new control test joins its first read producer and allows explicit reply backpressure when input consumes the whole business budget; it then verifies actual committed data under retained control waiters. Initial priority control scheduling rejected a command while status was busy; the unchanged archive commit-before-apply boundary exposed it. Command admission now waits for that check and producer continuation precedes metadata batches. Failed and temporary diagnostic outputs are retained separately. Numeric markers remain 1 and the current namespace identity remains cellar-raft-ltx-1/members-1/seeds-1/s3-1/repairs-1/nodes-1. No physical S3, power-loss, real failure-zone, production performance/capacity, larger tiers, federation or complete release qualification is claimed. Existing vendored warnings remain visible.",
